{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the nations shall bless themselves by your seed.</b> A person says to his son, 'May your seed be like the seed of Isaac' — and so throughout Scripture: ״וזה אב לכולן בך יברך ישראל לאמר ישמך וגו׳״ (Genesis 48:20). And likewise for cursing we find the same: ״והיתה האשה לאלה״ (Numbers 5) — the one cursing his enemy says, 'May you be like so-and-so.' And likewise ״והנחתם שמכם לשבועה לבחירי״ (Isaiah 65) — the one swearing says, 'May I be like so-and-so if I did such and such.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:36.973493572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}